---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// About — the publication-first story (rewritten 2026-07-07, D1 Option B).
// The engine methodology moved to /method; this page says what The Whetstone
// IS: a publication built on a structural-logic audit engine, and the three
// surfaces that engine powers.
---
<Base
  title="About - The Whetstone"
  description="The Whetstone is a publication: briefings that map the strongest positions on contested questions, with a structural audit of every position's reasoning. The same engine is free to run on anything."
  canonicalPath="/about"
  ogImage="/og/page-about.png"
>
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 sm:pt-20 pb-12 sm:pb-16">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-4">Audits the reasoning: not the source, not the facts, the argument itself</p>
          <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-ink-strong leading-[1.1] mb-6">
            Arguments,<br class="hidden sm:block" /> examined.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-5">
            The Whetstone is a publication: <a href="/" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent">briefings</a> that map where the strongest positions
            on a contested question stand, with a structural audit of every position's reasoning: named fallacies,
            unstated assumptions, terms doing hidden work.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-8">
            The same engine is free to run on anything at <a href="/audit" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent">the Audit</a>:
            Read mode audits what someone else wrote, <a href="/creator" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent">Create mode</a> points
            it at your own writing before your readers do.
          </p>
          <!-- The three-way contrast, moved here from the homepage launcher
               (L2 decision, 2026-08-05): positioning copy lives on the about
               page, not above the feed. -->
          <dl class="space-y-1.5 text-[15px] border-l-2 border-hairline pl-4 mb-8">
            <div class="flex gap-2.5"><dt class="text-muted w-28 shrink-0">Bias tools</dt><dd class="text-ink">rate the source.</dd></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2.5"><dt class="text-muted w-28 shrink-0">Fact-checkers</dt><dd class="text-ink">rate the claim.</dd></div>
            <div class="flex gap-2.5"><dt class="text-ink-strong font-medium w-28 shrink-0">The Whetstone</dt><dd class="text-ink-strong font-medium">audits the <span class="underline decoration-accent-support decoration-2 underline-offset-2">reasoning</span>.</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 sm:gap-4">
            <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 sm:px-6 py-3 bg-accent-support text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-accent-support/90 transition-colors">
              Read the briefings
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
            </a>
            <a href="/audit" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 sm:px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink border border-hairline rounded-lg hover:bg-paper transition-colors">
              Try the Audit, free
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Product mockup: show, don't tell -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-surface shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-hairline bg-paper">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-hairline"></span>
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-hairline"></span>
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-hairline"></span>
              <span class="ml-2 text-xs font-medium text-muted">The Whetstone audit</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 space-y-3">
              <p class="text-xs text-ink leading-relaxed font-serif">
                The experts who got us here are
                <mark class="bg-sev-med/10 border-b-2 border-sev-med rounded-none px-0.5">now telling us not to trust our own eyes</mark>.
                <mark class="bg-accent/10 border-b-2 border-accent rounded-none px-0.5">At what point do reasonable people simply stop listening?</mark>
              </p>
              <div class="rounded-none border border-hairline border-l-2 border-l-accent bg-surface p-3">
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-1.5">
                  <p class="font-serif text-xs font-semibold text-ink-strong">Ad Hominem</p>
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-[2px] border bg-logic-bg text-logic border-logic/30">Logic</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-[2px] text-accent">Critical</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink leading-relaxed">
                  Attacks the messenger's standing rather than engaging the claim: "the experts are compromised,
                  therefore wrong" doesn't follow.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted text-center">
            Every briefing position carries a card like this. <a href="/method" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent font-medium">How the audit works →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What a briefing is -->
    <section class="border-t border-hairline bg-surface">
      <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 sm:py-20">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-muted mb-3">What a briefing is</h2>
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed mb-4">
            One contested question. The strongest positions on it, quoted verbatim from real sources and mapped on an
            axis named for what actually divides them, not left vs right. Each position is followed by a structural
            audit card. Then the part no other outlet gives you: the assumption both sides quietly share, and an
            editor's view that takes a position openly and states the devil's advocate against it.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
            <a href="/briefing/minimum-wage-jobs" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support hover:text-accent">Read a live example →</a>
            <a href="/method#briefings" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support hover:text-accent">How a briefing is built →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Three ways to use the engine -->
    <section class="border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 sm:py-20">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-muted mb-8">The same engine, three ways</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <a href="/audit" class="group block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-6 hover:border-accent-support hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-muted mb-2">The Audit · Read</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink-strong group-hover:text-accent-support transition-colors mb-2">Audit any argument</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-3">Paste text or a URL and read the structure behind it. Free, no account required.</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support group-hover:text-accent">Open the Audit →</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/creator" class="group block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-6 hover:border-accent-support hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-accent-support mb-2">The Audit · Create</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink-strong group-hover:text-accent-support transition-colors mb-2">Stress-test your writing</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-3">The same engine on your own draft: counterarguments, citation audit, evidence check, revision tracking, inline highlights. Sign in only to keep your work.</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support group-hover:text-accent">Work on a draft →</p>
          </a>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-6">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-muted mb-2">Chrome extension</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink-strong mb-2">Audit as you read</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-3">Select a claim on any page and audit it in place. Highlights overlay the page itself. Coming to the Web Store.</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-muted">Coming soon</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">
          Plans and limits: <a href="/pricing" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent font-medium">Pricing →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Method + transparency pointer -->
    <section class="border-t border-hairline bg-surface">
      <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 sm:py-16">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest font-mono text-muted mb-3">The method, in the open</h2>
          <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The lenses, the labels, the verbatim-quote discipline, and what the engine deliberately won't do are
            documented on the method page, and every prompt and schema behind them is in the public repository.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
            <a href="/method" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support hover:text-accent">How the audit works →</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/Daniell-44/Whetstone" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support hover:text-accent">View on GitHub →</a>
            <a href="/feedback" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-support hover:text-accent">Send feedback →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
